* ============================================================================
* workspace_v3_selflocate.dts -- DTSHEMA 3 step 1 (owner-chartered 2026-08-11):
* opt-in v3 payloads carry FLAVOR plus DBFROOT/IDXROOT/LMDBROOT declarative
* lines, and a v3 load resolves its AREA entries against the PAYLOAD's roots,
* not the current environment (self-locating posture). Global SETPATH slots
* are never mutated; LMDBROOT is recorded-not-applied (owner: "lmdb only for
* disks" -- application chartered).
*
* Proof shape: save mcc_x64's posture as v3 into the catalog, then BREAK the
* environment on purpose (SETPATH to the default roots, where no MCC table
* lives) and load it back. Restoration despite the wrong environment IS the
* proof. Coexistence guard: WORKSPACE_MEMO must run green on the same build
* (v3 is opt-in; v2 producers and consumers stay untouched).
*
* Run: DO workspace_v3_selflocate  |  regression: REGRESSION RUN WORKSPACE_V3
* Markers: V3_T1 (STUDENTS row readable through the self-located load).
* RUNTIME-PROVEN 2026-08-11 (build 14:47:06) by hand before promotion: WSID M6,
* FLAVOR X64, both roots echoed, 13 areas restored from the wrong environment.
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

FORMULA "WS-V3-PROOF-BEGIN"

* --- environment-first: the save leg runs from the real x64 roots -----------
SETPATH DBF DBF/X64
SETPATH INDEXES INDEXES/X64
WORKSPACE CLOSE
WORKSPACE LOAD mcc_x64
WORKSPACE SAVE v3_regress MEMO V3
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- break the environment on purpose ---------------------------------------
SETPATH DBF DBF
SETPATH INDEXES INDEXES

* --- self-location: the payload's roots must find the tables ----------------
WORKSPACE LOAD v3_regress MEMO
SELECT 8
TOP
? "V3_T1_selflocated_students_row:" + (SID >= 1)

FORMULA "WS-V3-PROOF-END"

* --- teardown: close and restore the x64 disk environment -------------------
WORKSPACE CLOSE
SETPATH DBF DBF/X64
SETPATH INDEXES INDEXES/X64
